{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Sally in Continental Europe"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "E-mailing Vanessa"}, {"type": "position", "content": 10}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 10}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Present Continuous vs. Going To for the Future"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Present Continuous tense for things that are booked in the future.  This can be a hotel reservation or an appointment with a doctor.<br>  <br>You use <span class=\"italic\">Going to + verb</span> to talk about intentions. These are things you want to do in the future. There is no booking or appointment.<br>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Going To\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm coming back home to New York.<br>   <br>I'm taking a small tour with some nice people tomorrow.<br></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm going to call you soon. <br>   <br>John is going to arrive in Mexico any day now.<br></span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Zero Conditional"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use the Simple Present tense in a zero conditional sentence.<br> <br><span class=\"italic\">When</span> can often take the place of <span class=\"italic\">if</span>.<br>  <br>You can use the Imperative with a zero conditional sentence.<br>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you don't write, I get worried!   (Simple Present)<br>When you don't write, I get worried! "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you get a chance, come here. (Imperative)<br>When you get a chance, come here."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you like flowers, Holland is the country to visit.<br> When you like flowers, Holland is the country to visit."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "worried"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "feeling anxious and upset"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I get worried when you don't e-mail me!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le10ob10aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk to friends."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "a line or two"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "one or two written sentences"}, {"type": "